From 97a7f7b398124e47f3db94704fec74768ec57938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:09:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Layers: decide layer-4 dependency on the board (CR 613.8)

Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth's "each land is a Swamp" and Blood Moon's
"nonbasic lands are Mountains" both apply in layer 4. The state-blind
dependency relation made each depend on the other (each changes types,
each filter reads types), so the loop fell back to timestamp order and
Urborg made the Island a Swamp before Blood Moon took its ability away.

Under CR 613.8a Urborg's effect depends on Blood Moon's: setting
Urborg's subtype removes the ability that generates the effect (CR
305.7). Blood Moon's doesn't depend on Urborg's: adding Swamp changes
no land's nonbasic status.

The dependency relation now settles what the shape can't decide by
previewing the provider on a scratch board:
- existence: the provider removes the rules-text abilities generating
  the dependent (SetBasicLandType, SetChosenBasicLandType,
  RemoveAllAbilities), the exact set that feeds abilities_suppressed;
- what it applies to: a type change only counts when it actually
  changes the dependent's affected set.
A bucket with such a pair is applied one effect at a time, with the
dependencies re-decided after each application (CR 613.8c); other
buckets keep the fixed state-blind graph. The full and incremental
passes share one bucket applier, and the referenced-grant selector uses
the same relation for ordinary pairs.

Covers Blood Moon and Evil Presence (any subtype setter), either
timestamp order, Blanket of Night as the independent control, and
Urborg working again once Blood Moon leaves.

